---
description: >-
  State1 (with a `note right of`) transitioning to State2 (with a `note
  left of`), rendered under the ELK layout; guards against ELK reserving
  title-width space for a note group's label, which would push the states
  apart.
config:
  layout: elk
  fontFamily: courier
---
%% A note group's label is the note text, which is never painted as a title.
%% ELK must not reserve title width for it, or the note groups push the
%% states apart.
stateDiagram-v2
  State1: The state with a note
  note right of State1
  Important information! You can write
  notes.
  end note
  State1 --> State2 : With a label
  note left of State2 : This is the note
